WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:05.680
With Captain Marvel fresh off its box office-conquering
opening weekend, Marvel is already thinking

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.480
ahead to its next blockbuster,

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:15.580
"I like this one"

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.740
having just
dropped the official trailer for the superhero-infused

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.140
crossover event of the year.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.280
The new Avengers: Endgame clip is clearly
built to stoke fan anticipation.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:29.940
Every moment seems to have something important
to say, and comes with the potential of deeper

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:33.200
meanings, hidden explanations, and misleading
misdirections.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:37.500
Let's break it down and take a look at the
details you might've missed in the newest

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.500
Avengers: Endgame trailer.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:43.570
And just so we're all clear, potential and
rumored spoilers ahead… don't say we didn't

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:44.060
warn you.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:48.820
We've seen this before: the Avengers: Endgame
Super Bowl spot opened on a quick sequence

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:53.180
that sped through ten MCU characters, most
of whom had died or been snapped in Infinity

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:53.680
War.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.820
Everything was in black, white, and red all
over.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:00.360
This time around, the red-highlighted footage
is back, and also specifically highlights

00:01:00.379 --> 00:01:05.720
some different faces… like Tony Stark, Steve
Rogers, Thor, and Okoye... four characters

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:07.190
who did not get snapped.

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:11.220
It's pretty widely known that Avengers: Endgame
is the final movie in Chris Hemsworth, Robert

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.180
Downey Jr., and Chris Evans' Marvel Studios
contracts.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:17.660
That doesn't mean they're definitively done
with their characters...but if you're gonna

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:21.360
retire a role, you could do worse than saving
half the universe, you know?

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:24.520
Meanwhile, that red coloring still seems highly
symbolic.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.600
Red is often connected to blood and death.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:31.140
But, as we've theorized before, it could have
something to do with the red Reality Stone

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.680
and its possible usage in un-snapping the
world.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.960
Will that gem be instrumental in defeating
Thanos once and for all?

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:41.280
If this montage means what we think it might,
keep your eyes peeled for that scarlet stone...

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:45.920
One of the most exciting moments in the first
trailer was the arrival of Scott Lang at the

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:48.200
Avengers HQ with his Quantum-powered Ant-Van.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:52.100
While the presence of Lang in Endgame is a
pleasant if not a particularly surprising

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:56.650
revelation, one attention-getting moment occurred
when Cap and Black Widow ask each other about

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:57.640
what they're seeing:

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:58.700
"Is this an old message?”

00:01:58.960 --> 00:01:59.680
“Ant-Man?

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:00.740
Ant-Man?

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:01.820
I know you know that."

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:03.140
"It's the front door."

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:08.400
Many detail-oriented fans seized on her not-quite-answer
to suggest that the footage wasn't actually

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:08.920
live.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.000
The word "Archive" in the upper left corner
of the screen also led some to theorize that

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:18.320
perhaps the security camera clip was, in fact,
a very "old message"... and from a different

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:19.120
year entirely.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:22.920
In the new trailer, things seem to point toward
a post-snap arrival for Lang.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:27.160
Ant-Man features heavily throughout the trailer,
but one scene in particular shows a befuddled

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:31.460
Scott looking at a telephone pole plastered
with missing person posters.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.440
While this could be highlighting a particularly
active day for kidnappers, chances are the

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:39.560
scene puts Lang firmly after the snap as he
starts to piece together what happened.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:43.960
One of the biggest questions that's swirled
since the dust from Infinity War settled was

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:47.640
if, how, and when time travel would factor
into Avengers: Endgame.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:51.680
Ant-Man and the Wasp explored the potential
of the Quantum Realm, opening up the opportunity

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:55.410
for that mode of inter-dimensional transportation
to come into play in Endgame.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:59.540
And we know from that film's post-credits
scene that the Quantum Realm is entangled

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.400
with time travel in some way:

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.860
"And don't get sucked into a time vortex.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.040
We won't be able to save you."

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:10.220
And as this newest trailer seems to indicate,
it appears more and more likely that audiences

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:13.260
will be pulled around the MCU timeline in
Endgame.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:16.980
The Super Bowl spot showed clips of Liberty
Island surrounded by apparently abandoned

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:21.900
ships as well as Citi Field looking ominously
abandoned… and not just because the Mets

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.020
missed the playoffs again.

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:28.680
The Statue of Liberty showed up for a second
time in the new trailer, but so did another,

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.100
more interesting clip.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:33.940
Halfway through the trailer, we see a short
sequence of the Avengers' Quinjet coming out

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:38.220
of the clouds with a city in front of them,
except this time the buildings are all lit

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:38.720
up.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:42.080
Could they be celebrating getting the power
grid back on post-Decimation?

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.320
Or are we witnessing our heroic crew heading
back to the past?

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:49.400
A quick shot in the trailer shows a very angry
Nebula whipping out her swords and making

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:52.480
a run at an unseen foe, Papa Thanos, perhaps?

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:56.680
The likelihood of Nebula playing a key role
in the film is high, especially considering

00:03:56.689 --> 00:03:59.980
her crucial part in the original Infinity
Gauntlet comics event.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:04.080
But another interesting thing to notice about
the scene is the landscape behind her.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:08.060
The scenery is quite a mess of fire and flame
and even a little reminiscent of the battle

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.160
on Titan from Infinity War.

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:14.240
Of course, at the end of the previous Avengers
movie, we're not quite sure where Thanos ends

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:14.740
up.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.640
Some have suggested that his new home could
be anywhere from within the Soul Stone to

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:19.500
Wakanda itself.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:23.720
However, reports surfaced online that Disney
shareholders were allegedly shown a clip that

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:26.360
put the kibosh on either of those two theories.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:29.380
One more time for anyone who wasn't paying
attention earlier:

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:30.080
"spoiler alert."

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:30.940
Still here?

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:35.980
In the clip, Nebula reportedly says she knows
where Thanos is and, coupled with an energy

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:38.900
signature that's been picked up on out in
space, heads off to find him.

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:43.060
Could this clip of Nebula on a battle-torn
planet actually take place on the long-rumored

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:46.380
"Titan 2" that Thanos withdrew to after his
work was done?

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:50.260
One of the most glaring things missing from
Infinity War was the anxiously anticipated

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:53.200
reunion between Tony Stark and Steve Rogers.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:57.440
While the two leaders had technically buried
the hatchet thanks to Steve's letter and accompanying

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:01.920
emergency cell phone, bruised egos and hurt
feelings take a while to heal.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:06.060
Of course, a Thanos-level apocalypse goes
a long way toward helping a reconciliation

00:05:06.069 --> 00:05:10.160
occur, and it's hard not to believe that once
Cap and Iron Man got into the same room together,

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.420
they'd be able to figure things out one way
or another.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:16.980
The bigger question at this point is when
in the world, or off of the world, that meeting

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:17.990
will take place.

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:21.760
While the new trailer doesn't show the first
scene where they set eyes on each other, we

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:26.800
do at long last get a glimpse of the two brothers
in arms suited up, walking side by side, and

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:27.860
man does it feel good.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:30.880
And on that note… what are those special
suits for, anyway?

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:32.040
Quantum exploration?

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:32.760
Time travel?

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:33.380
Both?

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:38.260
Well, regardless, with Iron Man and Cap finally
together again, the world feels a little,

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:39.580
just a little, bit safer.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:42.440
Unless...this trailer is another misdirect.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:46.740
Like when Marvel revealed an Infinity War
trailer showing Hulk running alongside the

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:47.840
Avengers in Wakanda.

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:49.820
Which was a scene that never happened in the
film.

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:52.140
They wouldn't do that to us again… would
they?

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:53.220
Would they?

